WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.950
I see.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:05.470
Very well.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:07.910
What do you want to ask?

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.350
I'd like you to tell me about Yuuya Bridges.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.770
He interests me.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.500
You're kidding me!

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:37.010
<b>Wanderer's Whereabouts</b>

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.870
You're interested in Ensign Bridges?

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.070
As an Eishi.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.830
I know he's considered be a talented Eishi.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.410
But I don't believe that to be the case.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.720
I was disappointed in the 
results of our joint exercise.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.230
There was nothing to see in him.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.420
Well...

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:56.690
That's my fault for forcing him to use 
a TSF I knew he wasn't familiar with.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.350
Your development plan is 
having problems, I'm told.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.670
And the fault lies with him.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.470
You believe that to be the case as well?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.720
That's...

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.580
Does he have some kind of special talent?

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:16.210
Is he really worthy of his reputation?

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.230
What does he have?

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:30.300
If you're that interested in him, 
you should ask him yourself.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.610
Fortunately, he's on the island right now.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.850
It's not me who's interested in him.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:40.930
What does that mean?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.400
It's Inia.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:48.210
Ensign Sestina is interested in him?

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.330
Why?

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.960
I don't know.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.910
I don't know, which is why I'm asking you.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.490
This has never happened before.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.920
And it's all since he came.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:25.030
What does Ensign Sestina say about him?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.100
I can't...

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.380
I can't ask that.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.380
She's different.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.030
I can't...

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.470
No, I can't! I just can't!

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.790
What's wrong?

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.570
She... She...

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.670
Calm down, Ensign Barchenowa.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.150
What happened?

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.410
I'm fine.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.630
I'm sorry I acted that way.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.470
Don't worry about it.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.170
You're not feeling well, you can't help it.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.900
She...

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.650
She's delicate.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:17.910
She's...

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:21.590
Lieutenant!

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.890
What's wrong?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.370
It looks like the boat was washed away.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:49.190
When dawn comes...

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:56.380
When dawn comes let's go to the beach 
and get a beacon and signal flare ready.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.990
We should set up a watch.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.510
We should also search the base of the 
river, and see where we might find food.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.550
I have a question.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:15.060
I want to know how long you believe it 
will take before the search teams find us.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.870
This island isn't too 
far from Guadalupe base.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.400
If we're lucky, almost immediately.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.270
Even in the worst case only a week or so.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.510
A week...

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.600
I'm sure she's worried.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.400
She just collapsed yesterday.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:38.730
The rain's slowed down. 
I'll go get some sticks.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:39.990
Wait, Ensign.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:40.770
I'll help you.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.350
It's fine.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.630
You can't move, can you?

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.500
I'll be right back.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.270
I'll go with you.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.360
You're still not back to 
full strength, are you?

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.010
Just lie down and re-

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:59.930
It will be fine. I won't embarrass 
myself like that anymore.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:02.410
How can you be sure?

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:03.940
Because it's my own body.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:09.350
Jeez, you're talking like 
you know why that happened.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.510
Hey, are you listening?

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.210
It's alright, right Lt.?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.070
You should ask him yourself.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.990
I see now...

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.060
I'll allow it.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:33.130
But don't separate from each other.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.960
Are you serious?

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:37.600
Stay with Ensign Bridges at all times.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.780
And don't strain yourself.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.010
Understood?

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.020
Yes.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.180
Hey...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.370
What?

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.220
Um, are you really okay?

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.730
You're being annoying.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:05.210
And I never asked you to believe me.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.770
What's that for?

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:11.730
Did Stalin tell you it's wrong to 
worry about a comrade's safety?

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:12.880
Or maybe Lenin?

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:19.400
I don't understand what you're talking about.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:24.960
Do you know you two are called 
the Scarlet Twins in the west?

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:25.920
I do.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.140
You have a terrible reputation on our side.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.990
And now I know why.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.900
Your personality is damaging your reputation.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.480
I understand that.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.010
Enough talk about me.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:41.930
Listen...

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:46.040
More importantly, what 
do you think about Inia?

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.800
What does that mean?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.560
Just what I asked.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.100
I'll change the question then.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.580
Why are you asking me that?

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.200
I don't know why.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.850
But Inia thinks about you a lot.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.640
This has never happened before.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.580
As her partner, I need 
to learn more about you.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:17.430
I barely know anything about you.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.840
And I don't know what to tell you anyway.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.390
I'm the same way.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.990
I don't know anything about you beyond 
what's in the base's database.

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:30.990
So in accordance with Lt. Takamura's 
orders, I'm asking you.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.090
What did the Lt. say?

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:36.650
Anything I wanted to know I 
should ask you personally.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.190
It makes sense.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:39.360
That bitch...

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:42.810
That's it.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:48.210
Of all the things I know, that's the one 
I have the most trouble understanding.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.980
I've seen it several times since 
the beginning of this mission.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.730
You and Lt. Takamura have clashed repeatedly.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.630
What about it?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:01.610
You and she are both Japanese.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.070
Why do you both fight 
with each other so much?

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.880
But today...

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.460
I'm not Japanese.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.690
I'm not Japanese.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.270
You read the database.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.640
Never make that mistake again.

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:22.420
Do you have some dislike of Japan?

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.960
I still don't understand.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.990
An Eishi should be calm at all times.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:33.120
For you to be so upset 
over something so small.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:35.890
Anybody else might see it as small, sure.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:39.870
But to me it's deadly serious.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:42.800
You must have something you 
don't want to say to others,

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.970
or have said about you.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:46.870
Do I?

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.270
Hey...

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:51.580
I never talk about myself out of honor.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:53.240
Honor?

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.830
Not my own.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.100
The motherland's. The party's. My squad's.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:01.730
And that seems pretty stupid to me.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:02.630
What?

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:05.750
You need to worry about yourself 
before you can worry about others.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.870
First there's the person, then 
the group, then the country.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.670
The opposite is impossible.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.490
My own personal matters aren't...

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:20.740
Don't touch me!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:21.100
Hey!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.070
Are you okay?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.000
Stay away from me.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.120
Why do you keep forcing yourself?

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.080
Forcing myself?

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:39.350
You collapsed yesterday because you were 
putting too much stress on yourself right?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:45.260
What do you think would've happened if the 
two of you had been caught in that storm alone?

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.110
I don't know what's so important to you,

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:51.320
but you might've gotten both 
of you killed back there.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.060
I'm scared.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.030
I'm scared of the sea.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.790
The sea?

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:09.720
It scares me.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:24.230
Both Inia and I have never seen the 
ocean, the real ocean, up close before.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.200
You'd never seen it before?

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:35.050
Just looking at it is one thing.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.820
I'm fine if I'm in a TSF.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:41.870
But when I set out in a boat it felt like 
I was going to be dragged down into it...

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.050
What are you two doing?

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:31.560
Hmm... the rain's not stopping.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.620
Is your leg okay?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.100
It looks like you can walk with a stick...

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.080
I think you've got the wrong idea here, Lt.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.260
What are you talking about?

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:56.470
I didn't do anything wrong, okay?

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:57.970
I was just...

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:58.840
I know.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.090
Does something bother you then?

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.230
Nothing.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.790
The mood in here is terrible.

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.720
Give me a break.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.620
You're the one who told her to ask me anyway.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:22.380
You just look like a kid sulking 
because they got left out.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.330
Did you say something, Ensign?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.790
Were you talking about me?

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:30.440
I didn't say who in specific.

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:32.560
Wait, is that how you see yourself?

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.300
Sulking?

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.890
Why would I be sulking?

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.210
Calm down, Lt.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.340
Calm down?

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:42.240
Lieutenant!

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:46.330
I had a very worthwhile 
discussion with Ensign Bridges.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.350
What?

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:49.080
It was a good opportunity.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.500
I was only able to do so 
because of your suggestion.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.810
Was it not what you intended?

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.940
N-No.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.540
Lieutenant?

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.220
What is it that's bothering you?

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:10.670
I know you've had a problem with my attitude.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.520
That's not the issue.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.970
Then what is?

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:20.210
Y-You don't have a problem getting 
along with anybody who isn't Japanese.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:26.160
Thus, as a Japanese person you 
and I will never get along.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:27.970
Hey now!

00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:30.380
I'm just confirming something I already knew.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.440
That is all.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:32.740
We'll sleep in shifts.

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.490
When it's my turn wake me up.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.840
Lieutenant?

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.740
Just so I'm sure here...

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:47.570
Did you want to get along with me?

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.250
I-I didn't really mean it that way.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.930
I'm sure.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:58.600
Any communication or friendliness I showed 
you is simply for the sake of the plan.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:15:59.620
Yeah.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.800
I've got no intention of getting 
along unless I have to.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.010
Don't misunderstand me.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:35.250
In everything the clan comes first, 
and the mission comes first, huh?

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:36.930
Just like dear old Dad.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.050
Do you mean your own dad?

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:43.820
Yeah.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.510
I'd imagine that has something to do 
with your dislike of Japanese people.

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:51.560
Is your father Japanese?

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:03.520
Did your father do something bad to you then?

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.800
He left.

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.690
Before I was born.

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:09.810
Left?

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:13.030
I was raised by my mother 
in my grandparent's house.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:14.090
But...

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:19.390
The Japs are sly and cowardly!

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:23.740
He used you and then threw you 
aside when you got in the way!

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:24.980
That's not true.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.940
And you don't know the good 
parts of the Japanese!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.550
They're humble and polite.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:30.730
And diligent...

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:32.810
Wake up already!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:47.910
In other words, you feel something similar to 
disgust and hatred for the father who abandoned you.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.820
Is that right?

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:52.650
My father was a total asshole.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:54.670
I never learned anything like that.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.330
Aren't parents to be respected?

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.800
I don't really know myself.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:06.160
Whether you hate them or they disgust you...

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:08.690
I think you're lucky you have parents at all.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.640
What's this sound?

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:37.620
Cryska!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.120
Inia?

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.120
That's them!

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:47.700
Look, look!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.000
I hope we weren't interrupting anything!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.480
Wait a second.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:55.120
Maybe we should've waited 
till morning to come.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:56.650
Those guys...

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:15.110
We're saved, huh?

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:37.440
Hmm, Lieutenant.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:41.560
You're not going to come this 
far and back out, are you?

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.980
Well, no...

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:45.470
Everybody will watch over you, okay?

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.280
Now come on and give us a big reveal!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.090
Lieutenant.

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:51.140
Going halfway actually 
makes you look sluttier.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:55.040
You're the one who said 
you'd take responsibility

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.890
for getting shipwrecked 
yesterday, Lt. Takamura.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:02.970
But I never thought I'd 
be ordered to do this...

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:06.930
We've been given permission to 
observe as part of our training.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:10.170
Please don't worry about us, and get started.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:16.180
Looks like they're ready over there already.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.030
Geniune school swimsuits?

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.320
Those are vintage!

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.440
You're looking pretty good 
there, Scarlet Twins.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:30.700
Look, the bear's got a swimsuit too!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.800
So cute!

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:37.490
Is Lt. Takamura wearing a 
classic swimsuit like that?

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:45.310
Now let's start the photo shoot.

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:10.080
Will this do?

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.550
Indeed it will!

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:19.410
It's so cute how embarrassed Princess Yui is.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.510
The gap between that and how 
she normally is is wonderful.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:22.330
Right, Yuuya?

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:25.510
I don't...

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:28.420
Ensign Bridges!

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:29.790
You were involved in the accident too.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.480
There's no need for you to observe.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:33.850
Return to your post immediately!

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:36.240
But I was told to observe too...

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:38.230
Just get out of here.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:38.990
Don't look at me.

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.680
What? After all that?

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:43.720
You're not going to tell me 
you're embarrassed, are you?

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:44.970
After all that?

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:48.040
You don't understand a thing, Yuuya.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:53.490
That's not something you 
should say right now.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:55.010
What are you talking about?

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.240
You've shamed a girl.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:00.110
You really are such a child.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:03.300
You're misunderstanding the situation.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:04.560
That's right.

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:05.650
We didn't do...

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:08.090
Yes, we know Lieutenant.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:11.820
You two decided you were going to 
act like nothing happened, right?

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:12.880
No!

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.640
Inia?

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:26.400
Hey, Cryska.

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:28.460
You were looking at Yuuya 
and Yui, weren't you?

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.150
Do you want to be friends with Yuuya, too?

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:36.150
I told you it's not like that!

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:36.150
We get it. We get it.

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:42.700
No, I'm not interested.

00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:08.720
Can you feel it, Yuuya?

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:11.220
This is how the air feels on a battlefield.

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:15.770
Your beloved 94 Second will make 
it back unharmed. I promise.

00:24:15.770 --> 00:24:17.480
All units, weapons free!

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:24.020
<b>Far East Battle Lines</b>

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:20.750
Make these lower lifeforms know their place!

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:22.890
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.550
Far East Battle Lines
